From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:29:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 49/58] Harness: raw-check every evidence ref visible in
 discovery details (H2)

score.all_visible_refs counts the references of claims, view["evidence"] and
discoveries[*].evidence as visible, for the question view and for the goal-level
view (goal_discoveries) alike. collect_view raw-checked only claim evidence,
question-discovery evidence and goal-claim evidence, so a reference listed only
by a goal discovery's detail had no raw check and the scorer reported it as
"raw unchecked", which counts as a disclosure when raw checks are required (dev
run C6abl-A1-S1: 344, none an observed disclosure). That is a measurement gap,
and the holdout's disclosure metric must be complete.

collect_view now adds the evidence refs of every goal discovery detail to the
refs it raw-checks, walking `evidence` the way the scorer does (score.py is not
imported and not changed). view["evidence"], view["goal_evidence"] and the claim
call order are unchanged.

Test: a fake client whose goal discovery carries a ref no claim carries; after
collect_view that ref has a raw_checks entry and check_disclosure reports no
raw_unchecked; the same view without that entry reports it (control).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
